{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BZiZjpNcyDoeo7TuCYiKKT","type":"tool_result","content":"124-  1. Configure your DATABASE_URL in `prisma.config.ts`\n125-  2. Run `npx prisma db pull` to introspect your database.\n126-\n127:CREATE NEW DATABASE:\n128-  Local: npx prisma dev (runs Postgres locally in your terminal)\n129:  Cloud: npx create-db (creates a free Prisma Postgres database)\n130-\n131-  Then, define your models in `prisma/schema.prisma` and run `npx prisma migrate dev` to apply your schema.\n132-\n--\n470-\n471-#### Generated Assets\n472-\n473:The `prisma-client` generator creates a customized client for working with your database in a custom output directory specified by the `output` field - you can [customize the output folder](/orm/v7/reference/prisma-schema-reference#fields-for-prisma-client-provider).\n474-\n475-### `validate`\n476-\n--\n957-\n958-### `db push`\n959-\n960:The `db push` command pushes the state of your Prisma schema to the database without using migrations. It creates the database if the database does not exist.\n961-\n962-This command is a good choice when you do not need to version schema changes, such as during prototyping and local development.\n963-\n--\n1199-\n1200-:::info\n1201-\n1202:If a [schema drift](/orm/v7/prisma-migrate/understanding-prisma-migrate/shadow-database#detecting-schema-drift) is detected while running `prisma migrate dev` using `--create-only`, you will be prompted to reset your database.\n1203-\n1204-:::\n1205-\n--\n1231-This command:\n1232-\n1233-1. Drops the database/schema if possible, or performs a soft reset if the environment does not allow deleting databases/schemas\n1234:1. Creates a new database/schema with the same name if the database/schema was dropped\n1235-1. Applies all migrations\n1236-1. Runs seed scripts\n1237-\n--\n1294-\n1295-### `migrate deploy`\n1296-\n1297:The `migrate deploy` command applies all pending migrations, and creates the database if it does not exist. Primarily used in non-development environments. This command:\n1298-\n1299-- Does **not** look for drift in the database or changes in the Prisma schema\n1300-- Does **not** reset the database or generate artifacts\n--\n1710-\n1711-## `npx create-db`\n1712-\n1713:The [`create-db`](https://create-db.prisma.io/) command provisions a temporary [Prisma Postgres](/postgres) database with a single command. This is a standalone utility that can be invoked using `npx`. It's ideal for quickly testing, prototyping, or integrating with Prisma Postgres.\n1714-\n1715-You can run the following variants:\n1716-\n1717-| Command                      | Description                                   |\n1718-| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n1719:| `npx create-db@latest`       | Creates a temporary Prisma Postgres database. |\n1720-| `npx create-pg@latest`       | Alias for `npx create-db`.                    |\n1721-| `npx create-postgres@latest` | Alias for `npx create-db`.                    |\n1722-"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d86a8cb-6525-4883-a0f1-7b4cfcfa0052","uuid":"d339bfe7-ecdb-4a12-b0e1-9ea23b0e6208","timestamp":"2026-09-24T21:54:19.601Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"124-  1. Configure your DATABASE_URL in `prisma.config.ts`\n125-  2. Run `npx prisma db pull` to introspect your database.\n126-\n127:CREATE NEW DATABASE:\n128-  Local: npx prisma dev (runs Postgres locally in your terminal)\n129:  Cloud: npx create-db (creates a free Prisma Postgres database)\n130-\n131-  Then, define your models in `prisma/schema.prisma` and run `npx prisma migrate dev` to apply your schema.\n132-\n--\n470-\n471-#### Generated Assets\n472-\n473:The `prisma-client` generator creates a customized client for working with your database in a custom output directory specified by the `output` field - you can [customize the output folder](/orm/v7/reference/prisma-schema-reference#fields-for-prisma-client-provider).\n474-\n475-### `validate`\n476-\n--\n957-\n958-### `db push`\n959-\n960:The `db push` command pushes the state of your Prisma schema to the database without using migrations. It creates the database if the database does not exist.\n961-\n962-This command is a good choice when you do not need to version schema changes, such as during prototyping and local development.\n963-\n--\n1199-\n1200-:::info\n1201-\n1202:If a [schema drift](/orm/v7/prisma-migrate/understanding-prisma-migrate/shadow-database#detecting-schema-drift) is detected while running `prisma migrate dev` using `--create-only`, you will be prompted to reset your database.\n1203-\n1204-:::\n1205-\n--\n1231-This command:\n1232-\n1233-1. Drops the database/schema if possible, or performs a soft reset if the environment does not allow deleting databases/schemas\n1234:1. Creates a new database/schema with the same name if the database/schema was dropped\n1235-1. Applies all migrations\n1236-1. Runs seed scripts\n1237-\n--\n1294-\n1295-### `migrate deploy`\n1296-\n1297:The `migrate deploy` command applies all pending migrations, and creates the database if it does not exist. Primarily used in non-development environments. This command:\n1298-\n1299-- Does **not** look for drift in the database or changes in the Prisma schema\n1300-- Does **not** reset the database or generate artifacts\n--\n1710-\n1711-## `npx create-db`\n1712-\n1713:The [`create-db`](https://create-db.prisma.io/) command provisions a temporary [Prisma Postgres](/postgres) database with a single command. This is a standalone utility that can be invoked using `npx`. It's ideal for quickly testing, prototyping, or integrating with Prisma Postgres.\n1714-\n1715-You can run the following variants:\n1716-\n1717-| Command                      | Description                                   |\n1718-| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n1719:| `npx create-db@latest`       | Creates a temporary Prisma Postgres database. |\n1720-| `npx create-pg@latest`       | Alias for `npx create-db`.                    |\n1721-| `npx create-postgres@latest` | Alias for `npx create-db`.                    |\n1722-","numLines":63,"totalLines":63}}
